---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout title="Terms and Conditions — Nexus Wave Technologies">
  <section class="hero legal-hero"><div class="container post-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
    <h1>Terms and Conditions</h1>
    <p class="lead">These Terms explain how you may use the Nexus Wave Technologies website, community services, Women Safety support features and related Nexus services.</p>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="container legal-shell"><nav class="legal-nav" aria-label="Legal pages"><a href="/legal/privacy">Privacy</a><a href="/legal/terms">Terms</a><a href="/legal/refund">Refunds</a><a href="/legal/disclaimer">Disclaimer</a><a href="/legal/accessibility">Accessibility</a></nav><article class="prose card legal-document">
    <h2>1. Agreement</h2>
    <p>By using this website or a feature that references these Terms, you agree to use the service lawfully, respectfully and in a way that does not put other users or the service at unnecessary risk.</p>

    <h2>2. The website and Nexus services</h2>
    <p>The website provides public information, posts, utilities, community information, Women Safety reporting and other service entry points. Some services may require a Nexus Plus account or another verified contact method.</p>

    <h2>3. Public content and community use</h2>
    <p>Do not use the website to impersonate another person, harass someone, publish another person's private information, distribute malicious code, evade security controls, or abuse moderation and reporting systems.</p>

    <h2>4. Private Women Safety complaints</h2>
    <p>The Women Safety complaint channel is intended for people who need a private way to describe a concern and request support. It is not a public forum, not a social feed and not a method for exposing someone else's private information.</p>
    <p>A complaint receives a unique case number/code. Keep that number and any private invitation link confidential. Anyone who gains access to a valid private invitation may be able to attempt access to the associated support flow until the token expires or is revoked.</p>

    <h2>5. Contact requirements</h2>
    <p>Website-based complaints may require an email address or phone number when there is no authenticated Nexus Plus account through which a safe follow-up can be delivered. If you are already a Nexus Plus user and the system can securely match your verified account, the app-based contact route may be used instead.</p>

    <h2>6. Support worker access</h2>
    <p>Support access is case-scoped. A volunteer is not automatically entitled to browse a complainant's broader profile, account, friends, phone number, email history or community activity. Women-focused cases are intended for approved women support roles; men-focused cases are intended for approved men support roles.</p>

    <h2>7. Volunteer screening</h2>
    <p>Applying to help with Women Safety does not create an instant support role. Applicants may need an interview and screening process covering motivation, confidentiality, respectful communication, boundaries, safeguarding, escalation and technical procedures. Nexus may reject or suspend an application if these standards are not met.</p>

    <h2>8. Private communication</h2>
    <p>Where enabled, private case communication may use protected chat and WebRTC voice sessions. The service may use signaling metadata and case membership data to establish those sessions. Participants must not record, retransmit or publish a private support conversation without lawful authority or appropriate consent.</p>

    <h2>9. Encryption and security</h2>
    <p>Nexus uses security controls intended to protect personal information, including encrypted transport and restricted access. However, no online service can guarantee perfect security. Users must protect passwords, device access and private invitation links.</p>

    <h2>10. Case retention</h2>
    <p>Nexus follows a data-minimisation approach. Temporary data should be removed as soon as operationally unnecessary, and private complaint records are generally intended to be retained for up to 5 days unless a longer period is necessary for an active support process, legal compliance, security or another documented reason.</p>

    <h2>11. Prohibited submissions</h2>
    <p>Do not submit passwords, OTPs, banking credentials, private keys, malware, deliberately false emergency information, non-consensual intimate material, or personal information that you are not legally entitled to share.</p>

    <h2>12. Emergency limitations</h2>
    <p>The Women Safety service is an additional support pathway. It does not guarantee immediate response and does not replace emergency services, police, medical care or professional legal support. Response times may vary depending on the availability of approved support workers.</p>

    <h2>13. Complaints and abuse reports</h2>
    <p>You may report misuse of a profile or support workflow without being friends with the reported person. Deliberately false reports, harassment of volunteers, or attempts to obtain private data through the support system may result in suspension or other action.</p>

    <h2>14. Accounts and identity</h2>
    <p>Where account verification is required, you must provide accurate information and must not knowingly create duplicate or deceptive accounts to bypass safety controls. Verified phone authentication, risk checks and other controls may be used to reduce abuse and duplicate-account creation.</p>

    <h2>15. Nexus Plus migration</h2>
    <p>If a website complaint contact method later matches a verified Nexus Plus account, the support system may offer a transition to app-based communication. The purpose is to move the support conversation into the authenticated environment and reduce reliance on email or phone communication.</p>

    <h2>16. Notifications</h2>
    <p>Notifications may be used for case updates, support availability, security alerts and service information. Notification messages should contain only the minimum information needed to tell you that an update exists.</p>

    <h2>17. Third-party services</h2>
    <p>Some features may depend on Supabase, WebRTC-compatible infrastructure, email providers or other service providers. Service availability can therefore depend on systems outside Nexus's direct control.</p>

    <h2>18. Changes and availability</h2>
    <p>Features may change, be temporarily disabled, or be redesigned as safety and reliability requirements evolve. We may update these Terms when material changes are made.</p>

    <h2>19. No guarantee of outcome</h2>
    <p>The availability of a complaint channel or support worker does not guarantee a particular legal, medical, financial or safety outcome. Information provided by volunteers is intended as support and does not create a professional-client relationship unless a separate agreement expressly says otherwise.</p>

    <h2>20. Contact</h2>
    <p>Email: <a href="mailto:info@nexusweb.co.in">info@nexusweb.co.in</a></p>
    <p class="muted">Last updated: September 28, 2026.</p>
  </article></div></section>
<style is:global>
  .legal-hero{padding:72px 0 40px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-border);background:linear-gradient(180deg,var(--color-surface),var(--color-bg))}
  .legal-hero .lead{max-width:760px}
  .legal-shell{display:grid;grid-template-columns:220px minmax(0,1fr);gap:32px;align-items:start}
  .legal-nav{position:sticky;top:96px;display:grid;gap:6px;padding:8px;border:1px solid var(--color-border);border-radius:16px;background:var(--color-surface)}
  .legal-nav a{padding:10px 12px;border-radius:10px;color:var(--color-text-muted);text-decoration:none;font-size:.92rem;font-weight:650}
  .legal-nav a:hover,.legal-nav a[aria-current=page]{background:var(--color-surface-soft);color:var(--color-text)}
  .legal-document{padding:32px}
  .legal-document h2{margin:34px 0 10px;font-size:1.35rem}
  .legal-document h2:first-child{margin-top:0}
  .legal-document p{margin:0 0 14px;color:var(--color-text-muted);line-height:1.75}
  .legal-meta{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;margin-top:20px}
  .legal-meta span{padding:7px 10px;border:1px solid var(--color-border);border-radius:999px;font-size:.78rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--color-text-muted)}
  @media(max-width:850px){.legal-shell{grid-template-columns:1fr}.legal-nav{position:static;display:flex;overflow:auto}.legal-nav a{flex:0 0 auto}.legal-document{padding:24px}}
</style>
</Layout>